%S A399800 3,5,11,29,83,161053,-1,1174711139839,6563,2357947693,59051,
%T A399800 952809757913929,-1,1165087474585497590531113,4782971,14348909,-1,
%U A399800 762939453127,-1,4167894743351360316148563713643853057642190429160283,-1,394280051169577274041320687457275529031769961746269682997597789050649,-1
%N A399800 a(n) is the least prime of the form p^n + 2 where p is prime, or -1 if there is no such prime.
%C A399800 If n > 0 is even, then p^n + 2 is divisible by 3 for all primes p > 3, so a(n) is either 3^n + 2 (if that is prime, i.e. n is in A051783) or -1.
%H A399800 Robert Israel, <a href="/A399800/b399800.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..222</a>
%F A399800 a(n) = A087575(n)^n + 2 if A087575(n) > 0, else a(n) = -1.
%e A399800 a(5) = 161053 because 161053 = 11^5 + 2 where 11 and 161053 are prime, and nothing smaller works.
%p A399800 f:= proc(n) local p,q;
%p A399800    if n::even then if isprime(3^n+2) then return 3^n+2 else return -1 fi fi;
%p A399800    p:= 2;
%p A399800    do
%p A399800      p:= nextprime(p);
%p A399800      q:= p^n+2;
%p A399800      if isprime(q) then return q fi;
%p A399800   od;
%p A399800 end proc:
%p A399800 map(f, [$1..30]);
%Y A399800 Cf. A051783, A087575, A095302.
%K A399800 sign,new
%O A399800 0,1
%A A399800 _Robert Israel_, Oct 19 2026
